00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.810
Not surprisingly several
federal statutes make it illegal

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.210
to induce someone under the age of 18

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.560
to travel over state lines,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.790
to engage in sex in exchange for money,

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:00.950
or something of value.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.250
The main federal law is 8 U.S.C. 1591

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.460
which prohibits sex trafficking

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.720
of children by force fraud or coercion.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:07.940
And for purposes of this law,

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.840
a minor is someone under
the age of 18 years old.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.270
This statute also makes
it a federal offense

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.370
to knowingly recruit,
entice, harbor, transport,

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:17.070
provide, obtain, or
maintain a minor knowing

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.080
or in reckless disregard

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.560
of the fact that the victim is a minor

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.400
and would be caused to engage
in a commercial sex act.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.750
And that is defined exactly

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.070
the way you would think it was.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.800
Now section 1591 does not
require proof that either

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.900
the defendant or victim
crossed state lines

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.130
or international lines.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.690
The prosecuting officer
doesn't need to prove

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.020
the defendant used force threats

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.900
of force fraud or coercion.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.410
But if the victim was
between 14 and 17 years old

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.950
the penalty is a minimum sentence

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.710
of 10 years in prison up to life.

